Patch 54. After patch 53.

Every native install registered its prefix in the CMake user package registry
(~/.cmake/packages/rexglue, HKCU on Windows); patch 36 only kept cross builds out. All installs of
one SDK version carry the same version number whatever their patches, so find_package(rexglue)
can take any registered one: an install with an older series (another codegen_id), or one with
only Release installed, which a RelWithDebInfo or Debug consumer then links without a word
(CMake maps the missing configuration). On one desktop there were four, three of them other
tools' private installs, one in a temporary folder.

REXGLUE_REGISTER_PACKAGE is now OFF by default everywhere; an install that should be found that way
is configured with it ON. Consumers name the install (rexglue_DIR or CMAKE_PREFIX_PATH).

Test: a native install leaves ~/.cmake/packages/rexglue as it was; with the option ON it adds its
entry, as before.

Upstream: not proposed.

diff --git a/cmake/rexglue_install.cmake b/cmake/rexglue_install.cmake
index 08240d4..c664f52 100644
--- a/cmake/rexglue_install.cmake
+++ b/cmake/rexglue_install.cmake
@@ -154,15 +154,11 @@ install(EXPORT rexglueTargets
 # Windows: HKCU\Software\Kitware\CMake\Packages\rexglue  (REG_SZ, value name = MD5 hash)
 # Unix:    ~/.cmake/packages/rexglue/<hash>               (file containing prefix path)
 #
-# A cross build (Android) is not registered by default: a native configure of a consumer would
-# otherwise find it there and take the target's libraries.
-if(CMAKE_CROSSCOMPILING)
-    set(_rexglue_register_default OFF)
-else()
-    set(_rexglue_register_default ON)
-endif()
+# Not registered unless asked for (REXGLUE_REGISTER_PACKAGE=ON): every install of the same version
+# is an equal candidate there, so a consumer's configure could take any of them, an older patch
+# level, one with other configurations installed, or a cross build's target libraries.
 option(REXGLUE_REGISTER_PACKAGE
-    "Register the install in the CMake user package registry" ${_rexglue_register_default})
+    "Register the install in the CMake user package registry" OFF)
 if(REXGLUE_REGISTER_PACKAGE)
 install(CODE [[
     # Normalize path casing on Windows before hashing to avoid duplicate entries
